/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 3937 0 R
/T (Deforestation and Habitat Loss: Nickel mining has led to the clearing of 76,031 hectares of forest, with concessions covering 1,037,435 hectares, 68% of which overlap with forests in 2022. A study by the UMD \(University of Maryland\) estimated that 153,364 hectares were lost between 2001 and 2022. Indonesia accounts for 26.4% of global mining-related deforestation \(369,356 hectares from 2001 to 2020\), with 41.5% attributed to nickel mining.)
/E (Deforestation and Habitat Loss: Nickel mining has led to the clearing of 76,031 hectares of forest, with concessions covering 1,037,435 hectares, 68% of which overlap with forests in 2022. A study by the UMD \(University of Maryland\) estimated that 153,364 hectares were lost between 2001 and 2022. Indonesia accounts for 26.4% of global mining-related deforestation \(369,356 hectares from 2001 to 2020\), with 41.5% attributed to nickel mining.)
