/T (Carbon Storage and Biodiversity Risk: Nickel expansion poses a significant threat to High Carbon Stock \(HCS\) forests, resulting in the loss of 2.04 million metric tons of carbon storage in Halmahera alone. Additionally, six of the top 25 nickel deforestation concessions impact 27,693 hectares of Key Biodiversity Areas \(KBAs\), endangering species such as the Sulawesi hornbill.)
/E (Carbon Storage and Biodiversity Risk: Nickel expansion poses a significant threat to High Carbon Stock \(HCS\) forests, resulting in the loss of 2.04 million metric tons of carbon storage in Halmahera alone. Additionally, six of the top 25 nickel deforestation concessions impact 27,693 hectares of Key Biodiversity Areas \(KBAs\), endangering species such as the Sulawesi hornbill.)
