<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 3944 0 R
/T (Water Pollution Crisis: Water contamination has surged  since the 2020 export ban in many villages in resource-rich nickel regions. Industrial pollution has risen sharply in nickel-smelting areas, from 0% to 71% in North Konawe, 59% in Morowali, and 61% in Central Halmahera. Groundwater depletion is severe in Wawonii and Gebe Islands, while Akejira, Ake Kobe, and Sageyan Rivers show heavy pollution from erosion and deforestation.)
