/T (Limited Formal Employment Generation: Despite claims of local prosperity through job creation, nickel mining's capacity to shift employment towards the formal sector remains doubtful. Historically, the mining and quarrying sector has been a major source of informal work in Indonesia; and employment increases were observed following nickel export restrictions. However, nickel manufacturing, particularly within the Indonesian Weda Bay Industrial Park \(IWIP\) in North Maluku, shows promise for expanding formal manufacturing employment.)
