/T (Increase in Informal Non-agricultural Employment: North Maluku's manufacturing employment surpassed Sulawesi provinces, driven by nickel manufacturing and value addition policies. However, the establishment of the Indonesian Weda Bay Industrial Park \(IWIP\) in North Maluku has led to a rise in informal employment in non-agricultural sector, which raises concerns. Central Sulawesi has shown an increase in informal non-agricultural employment, challenging the expectation that new manufacturing firms would lead to more formal job opportunities. This paradox suggests a labor reallocation from agriculture to non-agriculture sectors due to the adverse effects of mining and manufacturing.)
