/P 3949 0 R
/T (Limited Impact of Nickel Mining on Poverty: The initial export restriction had a greater impact on poverty in mining-dominated regions, while the second ban compelled domestic manufacturing firms to sustain operations and employment, especially in regions with both nickel mining and manufacturing. Regions with substantial nickel mining and manufacturing outputs, such as Morowali, North Morowali, and Central Halmahera, showed a decline from median poverty rates within three years of the second policy. Areas with little to no nickel manufacturing activity did not exhibit similar improvements, except for East Halmahera. This suggests that nickel mining alone is insufficient to alleviate poverty due to negative externalities in agriculture.)
/E (Limited Impact of Nickel Mining on Poverty: The initial export restriction had a greater impact on poverty in mining-dominated regions, while the second ban compelled domestic manufacturing firms to sustain operations and employment, especially in regions with both nickel mining and manufacturing. Regions with substantial nickel mining and manufacturing outputs, such as Morowali, North Morowali, and Central Halmahera, showed a decline from median poverty rates within three years of the second policy. Areas with little to no nickel manufacturing activity did not exhibit similar improvements, except for East Halmahera. This suggests that nickel mining alone is insufficient to alleviate poverty due to negative externalities in agriculture.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [0]
