/P 3950 0 R
/T (Rising Agrarian Conflicts: Nickel mining and processing in Indonesia raise concerns about social costs related to unethical and unsafe practices. Land-grabbing infringes on Indigenous communities' rights through displacement and lack of free consent. Reports reveal inequitable land sales, intimidation, and compulsory excavation in Halmahera, with communities uninformed about land acquisition purposes. Agrarian conflicts in nickel extraction areas are rising, impacting thousands of families due to regulatory modifications and the classification of nickel mining companies under National Strategic Projects, leading to contentious land procurement.)
/E (Rising Agrarian Conflicts: Nickel mining and processing in Indonesia raise concerns about social costs related to unethical and unsafe practices. Land-grabbing infringes on Indigenous communities' rights through displacement and lack of free consent. Reports reveal inequitable land sales, intimidation, and compulsory excavation in Halmahera, with communities uninformed about land acquisition purposes. Agrarian conflicts in nickel extraction areas are rising, impacting thousands of families due to regulatory modifications and the classification of nickel mining companies under National Strategic Projects, leading to contentious land procurement.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 18 0 R
