/T (Ease of Doing Business: Indonesia needs to attract productive investment, which requires a regulatory streamlining to reduce investment barriers and bureaucratic hurdles. This initiative has been attempted with the formulation of Job Creation Law \(Law No. 6 of 2023\). This law has regulated several areas to attract more investment: investment climate and business activities; research and innovation; land procurement; economic zones; and national strategic project. This job creation law also affects the ease of doing business in nickel mining and industries. )
