/P 3955 0 R
/T (Revenue Sharing Funds: Indonesia has institutionalized the revenue sharing mechanism to regional governments through the Law No. 1/2022 \(Undang-Undang No.1/2022\). With a high revenue sharing rate to provincial and cities/regencies-level government \(80%\), these additional revenues should be utilized productively. Effective revenue management is necessary, considering the significant rise in local fiscal revenues from nickel-related activities. The use of revenue should be regulated for several allocations, including the expansion of productive sectors, compensation for affected people and/or sectors due to downstream process, and preparation for future transition. )
/E (Revenue Sharing Funds: Indonesia has institutionalized the revenue sharing mechanism to regional governments through the Law No. 1/2022 \(Undang-Undang No.1/2022\). With a high revenue sharing rate to provincial and cities/regencies-level government \(80%\), these additional revenues should be utilized productively. Effective revenue management is necessary, considering the significant rise in local fiscal revenues from nickel-related activities. The use of revenue should be regulated for several allocations, including the expansion of productive sectors, compensation for affected people and/or sectors due to downstream process, and preparation for future transition. )
