/P 3957 0 R
/T (Forest Protection: The Omnibus Law and its supporting regulations have significantly weakened forest protection in Indonesia, particularly for nickel downstream activities. Key provisions, such as the removal of DPR approval for forest designation changes, the simplification of permits into a single "business permit", and the centralization of authority in the central government, have facilitated easier access for both domestic and foreign companies to secure forest concessions. These regulatory changes, along with expedited permitting and reduced financial obligations, prioritize economic expansion over environmental sustainability, leading to increased deforestation and biodiversity loss.)
/E (Forest Protection: The Omnibus Law and its supporting regulations have significantly weakened forest protection in Indonesia, particularly for nickel downstream activities. Key provisions, such as the removal of DPR approval for forest designation changes, the simplification of permits into a single "business permit", and the centralization of authority in the central government, have facilitated easier access for both domestic and foreign companies to secure forest concessions. These regulatory changes, along with expedited permitting and reduced financial obligations, prioritize economic expansion over environmental sustainability, leading to increased deforestation and biodiversity loss.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [7]
