/T (Foreign Worker Permit: To streamline the employment of foreign labor, the Indonesian government eliminated the need for companies to obtain the IMTA \(Permit to Employ Foreign Workers\) and instead required only the legalization of the RPTKA \(Foreign Workers Utilization Plan\). This shift could weaken the regulatory structure, as the RPTKA is merely an administrative procedure compared to the IMTA's function as a tangible permit and inspection document. The absence of a mandatory IMTA may increase the number of low-skilled and undocumented foreign workers, intensifying competition for local jobs and potentially exacerbating social tensions.)
/E (Foreign Worker Permit: To streamline the employment of foreign labor, the Indonesian government eliminated the need for companies to obtain the IMTA \(Permit to Employ Foreign Workers\) and instead required only the legalization of the RPTKA \(Foreign Workers Utilization Plan\). This shift could weaken the regulatory structure, as the RPTKA is merely an administrative procedure compared to the IMTA's function as a tangible permit and inspection document. The absence of a mandatory IMTA may increase the number of low-skilled and undocumented foreign workers, intensifying competition for local jobs and potentially exacerbating social tensions.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [1]
