1382 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (The increase in regional fiscal revenue due to the nickel downstream activities has led to varied spending trends among nickel-rich provinces. Current expenditure has also increasedin these provinces, with most of the spending in 2024 allocated to personnel costs, except for North Maluku \(Figure 2.12\). The allocation for social assistance remains minimal across allregions. Capital expenditure characteristics differ among nickel-rich provinces, with only Central Sulawesi increasing its capital expenditure in recent years \(Figure 2.13\). While it is unclear whether capital expenditure is allocated productively, the allocation for capital goods may provide a more lasting benefit compared to current expenditure.)
/E (The increase in regional fiscal revenue due to the nickel downstream activities has led to varied spending trends among nickel-rich provinces. Current expenditure has also increasedin these provinces, with most of the spending in 2024 allocated to personnel costs, except for North Maluku \(Figure 2.12\). The allocation for social assistance remains minimal across allregions. Capital expenditure characteristics differ among nickel-rich provinces, with only Central Sulawesi increasing its capital expenditure in recent years \(Figure 2.13\). While it is unclear whether capital expenditure is allocated productively, the allocation for capital goods may provide a more lasting benefit compared to current expenditure.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
