/T (Nickel processing offers significant potential for expanding formal manufacturing employment. Following the initial export restriction in 2014, nickel-intensive regions saw a synchronous increase in manufacturing outputs, likely driven by the domestic processing of nickel ores. Initially, Sulawesi provinces led in manufacturing outputs after the surge in 2015. However, in 2020, North Maluku experienced a sharp increase coinciding with the reintroduction of the second export ban \(Figure 2.15\). This substantial expansion in manufacturing employment is likely due to operations within the newly established Indonesian Weda Bay Industrial Park \(IWIP\) in North Maluku. By 2021, IWIP reported employing over 24,000 workers since its establishment in 2018.)
/E (Nickel processing offers significant potential for expanding formal manufacturing employment. Following the initial export restriction in 2014, nickel-intensive regions saw a synchronous increase in manufacturing outputs, likely driven by the domestic processing of nickel ores. Initially, Sulawesi provinces led in manufacturing outputs after the surge in 2015. However, in 2020, North Maluku experienced a sharp increase coinciding with the reintroduction of the second export ban \(Figure 2.15\). This substantial expansion in manufacturing employment is likely due to operations within the newly established Indonesian Weda Bay Industrial Park \(IWIP\) in North Maluku. By 2021, IWIP reported employing over 24,000 workers since its establishment in 2018.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
