1632 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (The development of the nickel industry in the three major producing provinces has also impacted water quality. To proxy this, data from the statistics of Village Potential \(Potensi Desa/Podes\) can be used to assess environmental pollution at the village level in these provinces. Podes data is collected through field officers visiting each village or sub-district to gather information by interviewing key informants, such as village heads, local officials, or community leaders who have a deep understanding of local conditions. Villages are chosen as the unit of analysis because they are the smallest administrative units and are often directly affected by nickel mining and smelting activities. There is a noticeable upward trend in the number of villages experiencing water pollution, particularly in Southeast Sulawesi. This increase shows a significant spike in 2021, following the implementation of the export ban in 2020 \(Figure 2.24\). Additionally, the same figure indicates a rise in the percentage of villages affected by pollution from industrial activities, especially in 2021.)
/E (The development of the nickel industry in the three major producing provinces has also impacted water quality. To proxy this, data from the statistics of Village Potential \(Potensi Desa/Podes\) can be used to assess environmental pollution at the village level in these provinces. Podes data is collected through field officers visiting each village or sub-district to gather information by interviewing key informants, such as village heads, local officials, or community leaders who have a deep understanding of local conditions. Villages are chosen as the unit of analysis because they are the smallest administrative units and are often directly affected by nickel mining and smelting activities. There is a noticeable upward trend in the number of villages experiencing water pollution, particularly in Southeast Sulawesi. This increase shows a significant spike in 2021, following the implementation of the export ban in 2020 \(Figure 2.24\). Additionally, the same figure indicates a rise in the percentage of villages affected by pollution from industrial activities, especially in 2021.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 46 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
