1638 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (When examining the data at the regency level in each province, it is evident that both the percentage of villages affected by water pollution and the percentage of pollution caused by industrial activities have increased in most areas. This trend is particularly prominent in regencies with nickel mines and smelters. Areas outlined with brown dashed rectangles indicate regions with both nickel and smelters, while those outlined in green indicate regions with nickel only. Most of these areas have experienced an increase in both percentages, especially in pollution caused by industrial activities.)
/E (When examining the data at the regency level in each province, it is evident that both the percentage of villages affected by water pollution and the percentage of pollution caused by industrial activities have increased in most areas. This trend is particularly prominent in regencies with nickel mines and smelters. Areas outlined with brown dashed rectangles indicate regions with both nickel and smelters, while those outlined in green indicate regions with nickel only. Most of these areas have experienced an increase in both percentages, especially in pollution caused by industrial activities.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 46 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
