1644 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (The village of North Konawe, in Southeast Sulawesi, which has both mining and smelting operations, shows the highest increase in the percentage of water-polluted areas and industrial-related pollution. The percentage of polluted areas increased by 12% in 2021, while pollution due to industrial activities rose sharply from 0% in 2014 to 71% in 2021 \(Figure 2.25\). In Central Sulawesi, at the provincial level, the number of water-polluted villages has slightly decreased, and at the regency/city level, seven areas experienced a decrease. However, only one of these areas is a nickel-producing region. Notably, there was a significant increase in the percentage of villages affected by industrial-related water pollution in Morowali, an industrial hub, rising from 0% in 2014 to 59% in 2021 \(Figure 2.26\).)
/E (The village of North Konawe, in Southeast Sulawesi, which has both mining and smelting operations, shows the highest increase in the percentage of water-polluted areas and industrial-related pollution. The percentage of polluted areas increased by 12% in 2021, while pollution due to industrial activities rose sharply from 0% in 2014 to 71% in 2021 \(Figure 2.25\). In Central Sulawesi, at the provincial level, the number of water-polluted villages has slightly decreased, and at the regency/city level, seven areas experienced a decrease. However, only one of these areas is a nickel-producing region. Notably, there was a significant increase in the percentage of villages affected by industrial-related water pollution in Morowali, an industrial hub, rising from 0% in 2014 to 59% in 2021 \(Figure 2.26\).)
/Alt ()
/Pg 47 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
