1834 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (In North Maluku, the highest increase in the percentage of water-polluted villages occurred in East Halmahera, while the highest percentage of industrial-related water pollution was in Central Halmahera, jumping from 0% in 2014 to 61% in 2021 due to the development of the Weda Bay Industrial Park \(Figure 2.27\). This data also shows that many villages, which previously had 0% industrial-related water pollution, experienced a sharp increase in 2021 following the nickel export ban and the aggressive push for downstream processing. )
/E (In North Maluku, the highest increase in the percentage of water-polluted villages occurred in East Halmahera, while the highest percentage of industrial-related water pollution was in Central Halmahera, jumping from 0% in 2014 to 61% in 2021 due to the development of the Weda Bay Industrial Park \(Figure 2.27\). This data also shows that many villages, which previously had 0% industrial-related water pollution, experienced a sharp increase in 2021 following the nickel export ban and the aggressive push for downstream processing. )
/Alt ()
/Pg 48 0 R
/K [12 13]
>>
