1913 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (Nonetheless, this trend did not hold true for Central Sulawesi and North Maluku between 2019 and 2022 \(Figure 2.28\). Both provinces experienced an increase in the proportion of informal workers in non-agricultural sectors during the period of the second export ban, which is perplexing. In North Maluku, there was a sharp rise in informal employment within the non-agricultural sector following the establishment of IWIP. By 2021 and 2022, over half of the region's labor force engaged in non-agricultural activities was characterized by informal employment arrangements. Similarly, Central Sulawesi saw a slight increase in the proportion of informal employment in non-agricultural sectors throughout 2019 to 2022.)
/E (Nonetheless, this trend did not hold true for Central Sulawesi and North Maluku between 2019 and 2022 \(Figure 2.28\). Both provinces experienced an increase in the proportion of informal workers in non-agricultural sectors during the period of the second export ban, which is perplexing. In North Maluku, there was a sharp rise in informal employment within the non-agricultural sector following the establishment of IWIP. By 2021 and 2022, over half of the region's labor force engaged in non-agricultural activities was characterized by informal employment arrangements. Similarly, Central Sulawesi saw a slight increase in the proportion of informal employment in non-agricultural sectors throughout 2019 to 2022.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 50 0 R
/K [10]
>>
