1934 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (Despite the growth of the mining sector, open unemployment in nickel-rich regions remained high between 2019 and 2023 \(Figure 2.29\). This situation necessitates further resource-based industrialization that is more labor-intensive and can provide more jobs. The perceived employment opportunities in the mining sector may attract a large influx of workers from other areas, increasing the labor pool and potentially saturating the market. This influx can limit job availability, even as the mining sector expands, resulting in continued high unemployment rates.)
/E (Despite the growth of the mining sector, open unemployment in nickel-rich regions remained high between 2019 and 2023 \(Figure 2.29\). This situation necessitates further resource-based industrialization that is more labor-intensive and can provide more jobs. The perceived employment opportunities in the mining sector may attract a large influx of workers from other areas, increasing the labor pool and potentially saturating the market. This influx can limit job availability, even as the mining sector expands, resulting in continued high unemployment rates.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 52 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
