1936 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (Regions within nickel-rich provinces generally havepoverty rate higher than the national average. In 2014 and 2019, there was no significant improvement in median poverty rates, which remained around 14%. Compared to national average of 11% in 2014 and 9% in 2019, the median poverty rate in regions within the nickel-rich provinces are higher \(Figure 2.30\). This raises questions whether down streaming activities following the implementation of nickel export restrictions in 2014 had any effect on poverty alleviation. Specifically, during the initial five years post-regulation, only a limited number of nickel-mining regions experienced a reduction in poverty rates below the median, whereas the majority demonstrated minimal or no improvement. Even in Morowali, a primary hub for nickel manufacturing, the impact was marginal., a primary hub for nickel manufacturing, the impact was marginal.)
/E (Regions within nickel-rich provinces generally havepoverty rate higher than the national average. In 2014 and 2019, there was no significant improvement in median poverty rates, which remained around 14%. Compared to national average of 11% in 2014 and 9% in 2019, the median poverty rate in regions within the nickel-rich provinces are higher \(Figure 2.30\). This raises questions whether down streaming activities following the implementation of nickel export restrictions in 2014 had any effect on poverty alleviation. Specifically, during the initial five years post-regulation, only a limited number of nickel-mining regions experienced a reduction in poverty rates below the median, whereas the majority demonstrated minimal or no improvement. Even in Morowali, a primary hub for nickel manufacturing, the impact was marginal., a primary hub for nickel manufacturing, the impact was marginal.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 52 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
