1967 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (Our findings suggest two principal insights. First, nickel mining in isolation appears insufficient to alleviate poverty; while it provides some local employment effect. Within the first three years of the policy, regions with substantial nickel mining and manufacturing outputs, such as Morowali, North Morowali, and Central Halmahera, experienced a decline in regional median poverty rates. Conversely, areas with limited or no nickel manufacturing activity did not show similar improvements, except for East Halmahera. Despite these changes, the median poverty rates remain higher than the national average of 9% in, its negative externalities on agricultural livelihoods may offset its benefits. Conversely, a proactive nickel manufacturing sector could leverage a multiplier effect on the local economy, thereby contributing more substantially to poverty reduction. Second, the initial export restriction has exerted a greater influence on regions dominated by mining activities compared to those with significant nickel manufacturing, likely because the continued exportation of certain ores maintains incentives for mining output and employment. In contrast, the comprehensive second ban compels domestic manufacturing firms to sustain operations and employment, particularly in regions characterized by the presence of both nickel mining and manufacturing.)
/E (Our findings suggest two principal insights. First, nickel mining in isolation appears insufficient to alleviate poverty; while it provides some local employment effect. Within the first three years of the policy, regions with substantial nickel mining and manufacturing outputs, such as Morowali, North Morowali, and Central Halmahera, experienced a decline in regional median poverty rates. Conversely, areas with limited or no nickel manufacturing activity did not show similar improvements, except for East Halmahera. Despite these changes, the median poverty rates remain higher than the national average of 9% in, its negative externalities on agricultural livelihoods may offset its benefits. Conversely, a proactive nickel manufacturing sector could leverage a multiplier effect on the local economy, thereby contributing more substantially to poverty reduction. Second, the initial export restriction has exerted a greater influence on regions dominated by mining activities compared to those with significant nickel manufacturing, likely because the continued exportation of certain ores maintains incentives for mining output and employment. In contrast, the comprehensive second ban compels domestic manufacturing firms to sustain operations and employment, particularly in regions characterized by the presence of both nickel mining and manufacturing.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 55 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
1968 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (While our findings diverge somewhat from those reported by Mandala \(2014\), who observed an increase in poverty within nickel-rich provinces, we posit that these differences may be attributable to variations in data granularity. Our analysis leverages district-level data, which offers a more granular perspective on the localized impacts of nickel mining and manufacturing activities on poverty rates, in contrast to the province-level data utilized by Mandala \(2014\). This distinction may account for the observed differences in findings, and further research could usefully explore the nuances of these approaches to provide a more comprehensive understanding of the relationship between nickel mining and poverty dynamics.)
/E (While our findings diverge somewhat from those reported by Mandala \(2014\), who observed an increase in poverty within nickel-rich provinces, we posit that these differences may be attributable to variations in data granularity. Our analysis leverages district-level data, which offers a more granular perspective on the localized impacts of nickel mining and manufacturing activities on poverty rates, in contrast to the province-level data utilized by Mandala \(2014\). This distinction may account for the observed differences in findings, and further research could usefully explore the nuances of these approaches to provide a more comprehensive understanding of the relationship between nickel mining and poverty dynamics.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 55 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
