1970 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (A significant concern regarding nickel mining and downstream processing in Indonesia is the social costs associated with potentially unethical and unsafe land acquisition and operational practices. Numerous reports indicate that land-grabbing practices infringe upon the rights of Indigenous communities through forced displacement from settlements and farms, or by failing to secure their free, prior, and informed consent \(FPIC\). A recent report by Climate Rights International \(2024\) reveals that nickel industry development in Halmahera, North Maluku, has been characterized by inequitable land sales, intimidation of local populations, and compulsory land excavation. The report also documents instances where local communities were not informed of the intended purpose of land acquisition, indicating a lack of compliance with legal requirements mandating FPIC.)
/E (A significant concern regarding nickel mining and downstream processing in Indonesia is the social costs associated with potentially unethical and unsafe land acquisition and operational practices. Numerous reports indicate that land-grabbing practices infringe upon the rights of Indigenous communities through forced displacement from settlements and farms, or by failing to secure their free, prior, and informed consent \(FPIC\). A recent report by Climate Rights International \(2024\) reveals that nickel industry development in Halmahera, North Maluku, has been characterized by inequitable land sales, intimidation of local populations, and compulsory land excavation. The report also documents instances where local communities were not informed of the intended purpose of land acquisition, indicating a lack of compliance with legal requirements mandating FPIC.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 55 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
