1976 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (In 2023, the Agrarian Reform Consortium \(2023\) documented a rising trend of agrarian conflicts within nickel extraction areas, marking this sector as a substantial contributor to overall mining-related disputes \(Figure 2.32\). Specifically, the number of conflicts reported in these regions escalated from 3 in 2021 to 15 in 2023. Moreover, in the same year, conflicts linked to nickel extraction spanned an area of almost 50,000 hectares, impacting 36,137 families. Although the total conflict counts and land area affected may be comparatively lower than those in industries such as palm oil, the significant number of families impacted underscores that nickel concessions frequently occur in proximity to local settlements.)
/E (In 2023, the Agrarian Reform Consortium \(2023\) documented a rising trend of agrarian conflicts within nickel extraction areas, marking this sector as a substantial contributor to overall mining-related disputes \(Figure 2.32\). Specifically, the number of conflicts reported in these regions escalated from 3 in 2021 to 15 in 2023. Moreover, in the same year, conflicts linked to nickel extraction spanned an area of almost 50,000 hectares, impacting 36,137 families. Although the total conflict counts and land area affected may be comparatively lower than those in industries such as palm oil, the significant number of families impacted underscores that nickel concessions frequently occur in proximity to local settlements.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 56 0 R
/K [8]
