1992 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (Our preliminary conclusions in this chapter are derived from secondary data and qualitative assessments, suggesting a potentially skewed balance where the economic advantages of these activities are less pronounced than their considerably detrimental environmental and social consequences. While environmental concerns are addressed as a distinct category, we recognize their inherent interconnectedness with both economic and social spheres. The environmental impacts stemming from nickel mining and processing constitute a significant portion of our impact assessment, reflecting both the extensive real-world effects and the comprehensive documentation available. )
/E (Our preliminary conclusions in this chapter are derived from secondary data and qualitative assessments, suggesting a potentially skewed balance where the economic advantages of these activities are less pronounced than their considerably detrimental environmental and social consequences. While environmental concerns are addressed as a distinct category, we recognize their inherent interconnectedness with both economic and social spheres. The environmental impacts stemming from nickel mining and processing constitute a significant portion of our impact assessment, reflecting both the extensive real-world effects and the comprehensive documentation available. )
/Alt ()
/Pg 57 0 R
/K [8 9]
>>
