/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (We posit that the adverse consequences arising from nickel mining and processing operations may stem from the erosion of policy safeguards. Consequently, in this chapter, we attempt to establish a connection between the impacts detailed in the Chapter 2 and the policies governing three pertinent dimensions: economic, environmental, and social. It is important to recognize the potential intercorrelation among policies, whether within the same dimension or across different dimensions, as policy measures are often interconnected and can influence one another.)
/E (We posit that the adverse consequences arising from nickel mining and processing operations may stem from the erosion of policy safeguards. Consequently, in this chapter, we attempt to establish a connection between the impacts detailed in the Chapter 2 and the policies governing three pertinent dimensions: economic, environmental, and social. It is important to recognize the potential intercorrelation among policies, whether within the same dimension or across different dimensions, as policy measures are often interconnected and can influence one another.)
