2007 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (The Job Creation Law \(Kemenkomarves, 2023\) has introduced several measures to attract more investment. These include improvements in the investments climate and business activities; employment; protection of micro, small, and medium enterprises \(MSMEs\); support for research and innovation; securing land procurement; regulating economic zones and national strategic project; managing government administration; and ensuring law enforcement. Chapter III of the Law focuses on improving the investment climate and business activities. It discusses the simplification of basic and sectoral business permits and streamlining investment prerequisites, particularly in the mining and manufacturing sectors. While the mining sectors permits cover oil, coal, geothermal, and electricity, the manufacturing sector regulations simplify the rules for the resource-based industries. Chapter VI addresses the ease of doing business, introducing more flexible measures related to immigration, patents, taxation, and market regulation. )
/E (The Job Creation Law \(Kemenkomarves, 2023\) has introduced several measures to attract more investment. These include improvements in the investments climate and business activities; employment; protection of micro, small, and medium enterprises \(MSMEs\); support for research and innovation; securing land procurement; regulating economic zones and national strategic project; managing government administration; and ensuring law enforcement. Chapter III of the Law focuses on improving the investment climate and business activities. It discusses the simplification of basic and sectoral business permits and streamlining investment prerequisites, particularly in the mining and manufacturing sectors. While the mining sectors permits cover oil, coal, geothermal, and electricity, the manufacturing sector regulations simplify the rules for the resource-based industries. Chapter VI addresses the ease of doing business, introducing more flexible measures related to immigration, patents, taxation, and market regulation. )
/Alt ()
/Pg 58 0 R
/K [9 10]
>>
