2016 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (Indonesia has historically exported its nickel ore as a raw material. Given its substantial nickel reserves, Indonesia is determined to secure more value-added creation from its nickel resources. In 2014, Indonesia imposed its first export ban on nickel ore based on Law No.4 of 2009 on Mineral and Coal, which was then relaxed in 2017. The government implemented a stronger measure by imposing Law No.3/2020 on Mineral and Coal. This law also generally regulates the requirement for  nickel-related industries to prioritize local people in industrial and mining activities, and to establish and fund the community development program. Several regulations \(MEMR Regulation No.11/2019; Presidential Regulation No.109/2020; GR No.25/ 2024\) have also mandated the investors to build domestic smelters to secure the industrial value-added.)
/E (Indonesia has historically exported its nickel ore as a raw material. Given its substantial nickel reserves, Indonesia is determined to secure more value-added creation from its nickel resources. In 2014, Indonesia imposed its first export ban on nickel ore based on Law No.4 of 2009 on Mineral and Coal, which was then relaxed in 2017. The government implemented a stronger measure by imposing Law No.3/2020 on Mineral and Coal. This law also generally regulates the requirement for  nickel-related industries to prioritize local people in industrial and mining activities, and to establish and fund the community development program. Several regulations \(MEMR Regulation No.11/2019; Presidential Regulation No.109/2020; GR No.25/ 2024\) have also mandated the investors to build domestic smelters to secure the industrial value-added.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 59 0 R
/K [8 9]
>>
endobj
