2025 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (To achieve higher growth, Indonesia should consider engaging in a higher value-added industry, such as in the EV supply chain. The Indonesian government has formulated several industrial strategies to advance the downstream agenda to higher value-added process, including EV manufacturing, and Local Content Requirements \(LCR\). Through Presidential Regulation No. 79/2023 \(Peraturan Presiden/PP No.79/2023\), which revises the more ambitious targets set in PR No. 55/2019 \(Peraturan Presiden/PP No.55/2019\), the government has established  LCR  targets for EV cars at 40% of in 2026, 60% in 2029, and 80% afterward. However, this policy may not be effective if it is not supported by domestic production and infrastructure readiness. Therefore, there should be an alignment between LCR timeline and domestic production capacity. The government should also ensure the provision mechanism of the required infrastructure \(e.g. charging stations, renewable energy supply\). Additionally, this initiative also requires an in-depth cost-benefit analysis, to determine the cost-effective and most feasible production stage for Indonesia.)
/E (To achieve higher growth, Indonesia should consider engaging in a higher value-added industry, such as in the EV supply chain. The Indonesian government has formulated several industrial strategies to advance the downstream agenda to higher value-added process, including EV manufacturing, and Local Content Requirements \(LCR\). Through Presidential Regulation No. 79/2023 \(Peraturan Presiden/PP No.79/2023\), which revises the more ambitious targets set in PR No. 55/2019 \(Peraturan Presiden/PP No.55/2019\), the government has established  LCR  targets for EV cars at 40% of in 2026, 60% in 2029, and 80% afterward. However, this policy may not be effective if it is not supported by domestic production and infrastructure readiness. Therefore, there should be an alignment between LCR timeline and domestic production capacity. The government should also ensure the provision mechanism of the required infrastructure \(e.g. charging stations, renewable energy supply\). Additionally, this initiative also requires an in-depth cost-benefit analysis, to determine the cost-effective and most feasible production stage for Indonesia.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 60 0 R
/K [8 9]
>>
endobj
