/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (Moreover, the Omnibus Law has centralized AMDAL approvals under the Ministry of Environment. For example, in the mining sector, local governments no longer have licensing authority. The AMDAL Review Commission has been replaced by an Environmental Feasibility Assessment Team, which is now formed by the central government, whereas previously, governors, regents, or mayors could also form such teams based on their authority.)
/E (Moreover, the Omnibus Law has centralized AMDAL approvals under the Ministry of Environment. For example, in the mining sector, local governments no longer have licensing authority. The AMDAL Review Commission has been replaced by an Environmental Feasibility Assessment Team, which is now formed by the central government, whereas previously, governors, regents, or mayors could also form such teams based on their authority.)
