/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (Previously under Article 18\(2\) of Law No. 41/1999 on Forestry, there is a requirement to maintain at least 30% forest cover within watersheds and islands served as an essential environmental safeguard. However, this provision was removed under the Omnibus Law, making it easy to open forests near watersheds. Furthermore, the inclusion of Articles 110A and 110B in the Omnibus Law effectively provides amnesty for companies that have illegally operated in forest areas for years. By prioritizing administrative sanctions over criminal penalties, the law undermines the deterrent effect of environmental regulations, encouraging corporations to exploit forests. )
/E (Previously under Article 18\(2\) of Law No. 41/1999 on Forestry, there is a requirement to maintain at least 30% forest cover within watersheds and islands served as an essential environmental safeguard. However, this provision was removed under the Omnibus Law, making it easy to open forests near watersheds. Furthermore, the inclusion of Articles 110A and 110B in the Omnibus Law effectively provides amnesty for companies that have illegally operated in forest areas for years. By prioritizing administrative sanctions over criminal penalties, the law undermines the deterrent effect of environmental regulations, encouraging corporations to exploit forests. )
