/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (Article 10 of GR No. 43/2021 \(Article 10\) further weakens spatial planning by permitting PSN licensing and concessions to proceed even if they conflict with district and provincial land-use plans. This legal loophole has led to numerous cases of nickel concessions overlapping with critical forest areas, as companies no longer need to comply with regional spatial planning regulations. Furthermore, Article 19 of PR No. 58/2017 allows PSN locations that do not align with district/city spatial plans to receive a spatial alignment recommendation from the Minister of Agrarian Affairs and Spatial Planning \(Agraria dan Tata Ruang/ATR\), without requiring revisions at the local level.)
/E (Article 10 of GR No. 43/2021 \(Article 10\) further weakens spatial planning by permitting PSN licensing and concessions to proceed even if they conflict with district and provincial land-use plans. This legal loophole has led to numerous cases of nickel concessions overlapping with critical forest areas, as companies no longer need to comply with regional spatial planning regulations. Furthermore, Article 19 of PR No. 58/2017 allows PSN locations that do not align with district/city spatial plans to receive a spatial alignment recommendation from the Minister of Agrarian Affairs and Spatial Planning \(Agraria dan Tata Ruang/ATR\), without requiring revisions at the local level.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 66 0 R
