/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (Indonesia's ability to control air and water pollution has been further compromised by the removal of Article 102 of Law No. 32/2009 in the Omnibus Law. This change eliminates criminal sanctions for individuals handling hazardous and toxic waste \(B3\) without permits, thereby reducing accountability for environmental violations. Additionally, while marine water quality monitoring is crucial for pollution control, it remains limited to selected areas such as Jakarta Bay, Semarang Bay, and Benoa Bay \(AEER, 2023\). Meanwhile, nickel processing industrial zones in Central Sulawesi, Southeast Sulawesi, and North Maluku, despite their significant pollution risks, are not included in the priority monitoring areas. To mitigate these environmental threats, KLHK must extend its monitoring efforts to cover these high-risk regions.)
/E (Indonesia's ability to control air and water pollution has been further compromised by the removal of Article 102 of Law No. 32/2009 in the Omnibus Law. This change eliminates criminal sanctions for individuals handling hazardous and toxic waste \(B3\) without permits, thereby reducing accountability for environmental violations. Additionally, while marine water quality monitoring is crucial for pollution control, it remains limited to selected areas such as Jakarta Bay, Semarang Bay, and Benoa Bay \(AEER, 2023\). Meanwhile, nickel processing industrial zones in Central Sulawesi, Southeast Sulawesi, and North Maluku, despite their significant pollution risks, are not included in the priority monitoring areas. To mitigate these environmental threats, KLHK must extend its monitoring efforts to cover these high-risk regions.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 68 0 R
/K [5]
