/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (The lack of impact of nickel manufacturing on the increase in proportion of formal employment indicates a need for a detailed examination of corporate workforce recruitment strategies. Given the considerable investments by Chinese companies in the nickel downstream sector, it is unsurprising that these firms experience a significant influx of foreign labor from China to operate within nickel industrial areas predominantly managed by Chinese entities. In the context of IMIP, it is estimated that these companies employed 5,000 foreign workers from China as of 2020 \(Tritto, 2022\). The preference for foreign workers may be attributed to potential language barriers between management and employees, as well as the superior operational expertise they offer. )
/E (The lack of impact of nickel manufacturing on the increase in proportion of formal employment indicates a need for a detailed examination of corporate workforce recruitment strategies. Given the considerable investments by Chinese companies in the nickel downstream sector, it is unsurprising that these firms experience a significant influx of foreign labor from China to operate within nickel industrial areas predominantly managed by Chinese entities. In the context of IMIP, it is estimated that these companies employed 5,000 foreign workers from China as of 2020 \(Tritto, 2022\). The preference for foreign workers may be attributed to potential language barriers between management and employees, as well as the superior operational expertise they offer. )
/Alt ()
/Pg 69 0 R
/K [7 8]
>>
endobj
2125 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (Recognizing the imperative to expedite operational processes, the Indonesian Government enacted reforms to streamline the permitting procedure for foreign labor employment through the implementation of Presidential Regulation \(PR\) No. 20/2018 on Foreign Worker Utilization, which is later replaced by GR No. 34/2021 on Foreign Worker Utilization, a direct implementing regulation of the Omnibus Law on Job Creation in 2021, further revised in 2023. Under the new regulation, the government removes the obligation for companies planning to employ foreign workers to obtain Permit to Employ Foreign Workers \(Izin Mempekerjakan Tenaga Kerja Asing/IMTA\) and instead only requires companies to obtain legalization of Foreign Workers Utilization Plan \(Rencana Penggunaan Tenaga Kerja Asing/RPTKA\) \(Zainuddin et al., 2023\).)
/E (Recognizing the imperative to expedite operational processes, the Indonesian Government enacted reforms to streamline the permitting procedure for foreign labor employment through the implementation of Presidential Regulation \(PR\) No. 20/2018 on Foreign Worker Utilization, which is later replaced by GR No. 34/2021 on Foreign Worker Utilization, a direct implementing regulation of the Omnibus Law on Job Creation in 2021, further revised in 2023. Under the new regulation, the government removes the obligation for companies planning to employ foreign workers to obtain Permit to Employ Foreign Workers \(Izin Mempekerjakan Tenaga Kerja Asing/IMTA\) and instead only requires companies to obtain legalization of Foreign Workers Utilization Plan \(Rencana Penggunaan Tenaga Kerja Asing/RPTKA\) \(Zainuddin et al., 2023\).)
/Alt ()
/Pg 69 0 R
