/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (Zainuddin et al. \(2023\) highlight a key difference in the legal standing of IMTA and RPTKA, noting that the RPTKA is part of the administrative procedure while the IMTA is the resulting output. This distinction suggests a potentially weaker regulatory structure for the RPTKA, which could diminish the effectiveness of screening out lower-skilled foreign workers. The IMTA also functions as a crucial document for inspecting foreign worker entry. Therefore, the absence of mandatory IMTA could lead to an increased number of undocumented foreign workers, potentially intensifying competition for local employment and worsening existing social tensions between companies and local communities. )
/E (Zainuddin et al. \(2023\) highlight a key difference in the legal standing of IMTA and RPTKA, noting that the RPTKA is part of the administrative procedure while the IMTA is the resulting output. This distinction suggests a potentially weaker regulatory structure for the RPTKA, which could diminish the effectiveness of screening out lower-skilled foreign workers. The IMTA also functions as a crucial document for inspecting foreign worker entry. Therefore, the absence of mandatory IMTA could lead to an increased number of undocumented foreign workers, potentially intensifying competition for local employment and worsening existing social tensions between companies and local communities. )
/Alt ()
