/T (The state requires both nickel mining and processing industry to adhere to the MoEMR Regulation No. 26/2018 regarding safety provision, which stipulates the requirement for the companies to provide safety equipment for workers, establish clear safety governance and perform regular audit. However, as explained in the previous section, the persistent incidence of workplace hazards, coupled with multiple reports of substandard work environments within nickel manufacturing companies, suggests a critical deficiency in the implementation of Occupational Safety and Health \(OSH\) standards, as well as inadequate regulatory enforcement and monitoring mechanisms.)
/E (The state requires both nickel mining and processing industry to adhere to the MoEMR Regulation No. 26/2018 regarding safety provision, which stipulates the requirement for the companies to provide safety equipment for workers, establish clear safety governance and perform regular audit. However, as explained in the previous section, the persistent incidence of workplace hazards, coupled with multiple reports of substandard work environments within nickel manufacturing companies, suggests a critical deficiency in the implementation of Occupational Safety and Health \(OSH\) standards, as well as inadequate regulatory enforcement and monitoring mechanisms.)
