2137 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (In this chapter, we conclude that Indonesia is currently at a crossroads in its efforts to enhance the investment climate. The introduction of the Omnibus Law and National Strategic Projects \(PSN\) were intended to stimulate investment, economic growth, and job creation. However, our analysis reveals that these policies have significantly reshaped the landscape, often resulting in adverse social and economic consequences in the pursuit of investment and value-added policies. While some regulations showed promise, their implementation has not met expectations.)
/E (In this chapter, we conclude that Indonesia is currently at a crossroads in its efforts to enhance the investment climate. The introduction of the Omnibus Law and National Strategic Projects \(PSN\) were intended to stimulate investment, economic growth, and job creation. However, our analysis reveals that these policies have significantly reshaped the landscape, often resulting in adverse social and economic consequences in the pursuit of investment and value-added policies. While some regulations showed promise, their implementation has not met expectations.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 70 0 R
/K [7]
>>
