/E (Mexico: In 2023, Mexico reformed its Mining Law, National Waters Law, LGEEPA, and LGPGIR, tightening regulations. Mining concessions were reduced from 50 to 30 years, require prior permits, and no longer grant automatic land access. Companies must pay 5% of net profits to affected communities and face criminal liability for violations. Mining in protected areas is banned, industrial water use can be restricted, and concession holders now bear permanent responsibility for mining waste.)
/Pg 73 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
