/E (Germany: The Supply Chain Act in Germany obligates companies to implement due diligence by identifying, assessing and prioritizing risks in their supply chain. Companies are required to publish policy statements, set out measures to minimize violations in human rights, and establish channels for complaints. The legislation seeks to foster fair and responsible production by obligating companies to uphold robust occupational safety and health standards, guarantee fair wages and the right to unionize, and prevent unjust land acquisition practices.)
/Pg 73 0 R
/K [10]
