2210 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 4012 0 R
/T (Strengthening Law Enforcement and End Corporate Amnesty: Articles 110A and 110B of the Omnibus Law, which effectively provide amnesty for illegal deforestation, must be repealed. Instead, stricter criminal penalties and liability measures should be reintroduced to deter corporate misconduct. Companies engaged in illegal deforestation should face severe financial penalties, operational suspensions, and legal prosecution to ensure accountability.)
/E (Strengthening Law Enforcement and End Corporate Amnesty: Articles 110A and 110B of the Omnibus Law, which effectively provide amnesty for illegal deforestation, must be repealed. Instead, stricter criminal penalties and liability measures should be reintroduced to deter corporate misconduct. Companies engaged in illegal deforestation should face severe financial penalties, operational suspensions, and legal prosecution to ensure accountability.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 76 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
2211 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 4013 0 R
/T (Restoring Local Government Oversight and Public Participation: Current laws exclude local governments and forest managers from decision-making, allowing uncontrolled expansion of nickel concessions. To address this, the authority over forest management should be decentralized. This would give local governments, indigenous communities, and environmental organizations a greater role in monitoring and decision-making. Strengthening local participation will enhance accountability and improve enforcement of forest conservation policies.)
/E (Restoring Local Government Oversight and Public Participation: Current laws exclude local governments and forest managers from decision-making, allowing uncontrolled expansion of nickel concessions. To address this, the authority over forest management should be decentralized. This would give local governments, indigenous communities, and environmental organizations a greater role in monitoring and decision-making. Strengthening local participation will enhance accountability and improve enforcement of forest conservation policies.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 76 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
2212 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 4014 0 R
/T (Reinstating and Strengthening Legal Limits on Forest Conversion: The 30% forest cover rule for watersheds and islands, which was removed under Law No. 6/2023 on Job Creation, must be reinstated and strictly enforced to prevent large-scale deforestation. Additionally, land conversion of protected forests and High Carbon Stock \(HCS\) areas must be explicitly prohibited, even for National Strategic Projects \(PSN\), to ensure that ecological integrity is maintained.)
/E (Reinstating and Strengthening Legal Limits on Forest Conversion: The 30% forest cover rule for watersheds and islands, which was removed under Law No. 6/2023 on Job Creation, must be reinstated and strictly enforced to prevent large-scale deforestation. Additionally, land conversion of protected forests and High Carbon Stock \(HCS\) areas must be explicitly prohibited, even for National Strategic Projects \(PSN\), to ensure that ecological integrity is maintained.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 76 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
2213 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 4015 0 R
/T (Enforcing Reclamation and Post-Mining Restoration: Although nickel mining currently does not have abandoned sites, we can learn from the coal mining practices. Stronger enforcement mechanisms must be implemented to ensure that mining companies fulfill their reclamation and post-mining restoration obligations. Harsher penalties should be imposed on companies that fail to rehabilitate deforested areas, making ecosystem restoration a mandatory and enforceable condition of mining permits.)
/E (Enforcing Reclamation and Post-Mining Restoration: Although nickel mining currently does not have abandoned sites, we can learn from the coal mining practices. Stronger enforcement mechanisms must be implemented to ensure that mining companies fulfill their reclamation and post-mining restoration obligations. Harsher penalties should be imposed on companies that fail to rehabilitate deforested areas, making ecosystem restoration a mandatory and enforceable condition of mining permits.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 76 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
