/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 4017 0 R
/T (Banning Deep Sea Tailing Placement \(DSTP\) and Ocean Dumping of Mining Waste: Despite Government Regulation No. 22/2021 setting specific requirements for DSTP, leakages and violations of water quality standards have repeatedly occurred in practice, threatening marine ecosystems and local livelihoods. Numerous cases of pipeline leaks and contamination exceeding legal limits have been recorded, proving the risks of DSTP. Given that most countries have already banned this practice and following the precautionary principle, Indonesia should prohibit DSTP entirely to prevent further environmental damage. Government can focus on enhancing the practice of tailing management by confining tailings in tailings storage facilities \(TSFs\) in the form of dams. Solid-liquid recovery of mine tailings is an excellent approach to improve mining operations' sustainability and circularity and ensure cleaner environments. )
/E (Banning Deep Sea Tailing Placement \(DSTP\) and Ocean Dumping of Mining Waste: Despite Government Regulation No. 22/2021 setting specific requirements for DSTP, leakages and violations of water quality standards have repeatedly occurred in practice, threatening marine ecosystems and local livelihoods. Numerous cases of pipeline leaks and contamination exceeding legal limits have been recorded, proving the risks of DSTP. Given that most countries have already banned this practice and following the precautionary principle, Indonesia should prohibit DSTP entirely to prevent further environmental damage. Government can focus on enhancing the practice of tailing management by confining tailings in tailings storage facilities \(TSFs\) in the form of dams. Solid-liquid recovery of mine tailings is an excellent approach to improve mining operations' sustainability and circularity and ensure cleaner environments. )
/Alt ()
/Pg 77 0 R
/K [5 6]
>>
