/P 4020 0 R
/T (Preventing Local Job Displacement by Regulating Low-Skilled Foreign Workers: To mitigate the risk of local job displacement caused by the influx of low-skilled foreign workers, it is essential to introduce additional provisions alongside the RPTKA \(Foreign Workers Utilization Plan\). These measures could include setting quotas for low-skilled foreign workers and implementing, monitoring and evaluation mechanisms to ensure compliance and effectiveness. By reducing social friction, this restriction may also indirectly encourage firms to prioritize hiring higher skilled workers, thereby fostering knowledge spillover. )
/E (Preventing Local Job Displacement by Regulating Low-Skilled Foreign Workers: To mitigate the risk of local job displacement caused by the influx of low-skilled foreign workers, it is essential to introduce additional provisions alongside the RPTKA \(Foreign Workers Utilization Plan\). These measures could include setting quotas for low-skilled foreign workers and implementing, monitoring and evaluation mechanisms to ensure compliance and effectiveness. By reducing social friction, this restriction may also indirectly encourage firms to prioritize hiring higher skilled workers, thereby fostering knowledge spillover. )
